{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"printf '\\\\n--- PLAN FIELDS ---\\\\n'; jq 'keys, (.queries | length), .queries[-2:]' reference_query_plan.json; printf '\\\\n--- GLOBAL SUMMARY ---\\\\n'; cat global_memory_summary.md; printf '\\\\n--- DRAFT TARGET LOCATIONS ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'section|Rasch|logistic|Open LLM|Liang2023|Andersen1970|local IRT|item information' paper.tex; printf '\\\\n--- PROVENANCE SHAPE ---\\\\n'; jq 'type, (if type == \\\"object\\\" then keys else length end)' references_provenance.json; printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY LOG GUIDANCE ---\\\\n'; sed -n '65,145p' .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md; printf '\\\\n--- WORKSPACE STATUS ---\\\\n'; git status --short; printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY FILES ---\\\\n'; ls -l memory.md conclusions.md global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"printf '\\\\n--- PLAN FIELDS ---\\\\n'; jq 'keys, (.queries | length), .queries[-2:]' reference_query_plan.json; printf '\\\\n--- GLOBAL SUMMARY ---\\\\n'; cat global_memory_summary.md; printf '\\\\n--- DRAFT TARGET LOCATIONS ---\\\\n'; rg -n 'section|Rasch|logistic|Open LLM|Liang2023|Andersen1970|local IRT|item information' paper.tex; printf '\\\\n--- PROVENANCE SHAPE ---\\\\n'; jq 'type, (if type == \\\"object\\\" then keys else length end)' references_provenance.json; printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY LOG GUIDANCE ---\\\\n'; sed -n '65,145p' .codex/skills/memory-log/SKILL.md; printf '\\\\n--- WORKSPACE STATUS ---\\\\n'; git status --short; printf '\\\\n--- MEMORY FILES ---\\\\n'; ls -l memory.md conclusions.md global_memory/memory.md global_memory/memory.jsonl .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\"","aggregated_output":"\n--- PLAN FIELDS ---\n[\n  \"architectural_shifts\",\n  \"benchmarks\",\n  \"central_topic\",\n  \"comparators\",\n  \"core_methods\",\n  \"failure_reason\",\n  \"forbidden_query_patterns\",\n  \"queries\",\n  \"result_driven_themes\",\n  \"status\"\n]\n10\n[\n  {\n    \"query\": \"Holistic Evaluation of Language Models HELM\",\n    \"category\": \"benchmark_context\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Permitted starter reference for the source evaluation framework underlying six final benchmark matrices; cite dataset context without treating framework-wide claims or the raw upstream release as properties of the staged fixed item universes.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"query\": \"Open LLM Leaderboard v2 Fourrier Habib Lozovskaya Szafer Wolf\",\n    \"category\": \"benchmark_context\",\n    \"rationale\": \"Permitted starter reference for the leaderboard context underlying the development matrices and four final matrices; future retrieval must verify benchmark-specific provenance rather than assume every staged case is an official v2 component.\"\n  }\n]\n\n--- GLOBAL SUMMARY ---\n# Global Memory Summary\n\nUse as qualitative context only; do not use as quantitative grounding source.\n\n## Recent Entries\n\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Lineage-Held-Out Anchor-Audit Residual Estimation. gate=updated; trigger=b; reason=Supplied identity and explicit ancestry metadata enable an auditable grouped stress-test category absent from the empty conclusions.\n  - evidence: Mounted README documents repeated identities/details repositories, explicit Base Model metadata, verified columns, and no provided groups or scores. Bootstrap manifest reports correct=true and combined_score=0.9414127869558047; named candidate source path was unavailable. No new experiment or score. Considered richer IRT-only prediction, pure random sampling, and protocol-only work; selected a bounded source-prediction plus uniform-residual-audit intervention with conditional unbiasedness only at the raw full-correction endpoint.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-13T17:17:14.928338+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.9444775970444405, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"anchor_mae\": 0.24719956291422063, \"combined_score\": 0.9444775970444405, \"constant_mae\": 0.2100909190340938, \"control_failure_rate\": 0.0, \"copy_mae\": 0.1778997763664952, \"correct\": false, \"delta_anchor_ci_high\": 1.0, \"delta_anchor_ci_low\": -1.0, \"delta_anchor_mae\": -0.19167715995866108, \"irt_mae\": 0.04121063683083198, \"kendall_tau_b\": 0.6472179218700796, \"mae\": 0.05552240295555956, \"missing_episode_rate\": 0.0, \"no_calibration_mae\": 0.11230918829448545, \"no_diversity_mae\": 0.060846081878834724, \"permuted_mae\": 0.1294150243149829, \"reset_mae\": 0.04647316766485056, \"reset_max_abs_error\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.06878752313066207, \"source_mean_mae\": 0.12786232844772225, \"spearman\": 0.8092089396608806, \"uniform_mae\": 0.09894661693226534}\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Score-Targeted Covariance Design with Group-Held-Out Calibration: direct full-score conditional-variance acquisition, equal source-group training weights, and source-only nested calibration. gate=updated; trigger=d; reason=Qualify the ancestry-stress-test recommendation to distinguish offline metadata from the documented opaque-source-group-only candidate interface, and distinguish recorded aggregate underperformance against IRT from an unknown acceptance-failure cause.\n  - evidence: Historical interface memory documents opaque source_groups, nested 8/16/32 prefixes, and no target full scores or target groups. Historical candidate MAE=0.05552240295555956 versus reported IRT MAE=0.04121063683083198; calibration/diversity ablations were numerically worse. Historical combined_score=0.9444775970444405 with correct=false did not establish acceptance or its failure cause; accepted bootstrap remains combined_score=0.9414127869558047 with correct=true. Considered another residual audit, richer latent reconstruction, protocol-only changes, and direct score-risk acquisition; selected the last as a bounded observable-only mechanism admitting a same-predictor D-optimal ablation. No new computation, measurement, or forbidden literature access.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-13T17:35:03.901393+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.9649669664663327, correct=False; scientific acceptance failed; cause unavailable; correct=false alone does not establish a protocol or implementation defect; search metrics (data): {\"anchor_mae\": 0.24719956291422063, \"combined_score\": 0.9649669664663327, \"constant_mae\": 0.19445070209615578, \"control_failure_rate\": 0.0, \"copy_mae\": 0.19343264686385855, \"correct\": false, \"delta_anchor_ci_high\": 1.0, \"delta_anchor_ci_low\": -1.0, \"delta_anchor_mae\": -0.2121665293805533, \"irt_mae\": 0.04121063683083198, \"kendall_tau_b\": 0.720911927988862, \"mae\": 0.0350330335336673, \"missing_episode_rate\": 0.0, \"no_calibration_mae\": 0.03464729153264736, \"no_diversity_mae\": 0.05351526989144261, \"permuted_mae\": 0.12148785819970097, \"reset_mae\": 0.03602846597539919, \"reset_max_abs_error\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.04484693916622435, \"source_mean_mae\": 0.12786232844772225, \"spearman\": 0.8644226555576705, \"uniform_mae\": 0.09894661693226534}\n- 2026-11-13 | step=idea | scope=idea\n  - summary: Wrote Rasch-Residual Profile Mixtures on Fixed Score-Targeted Prefixes. gate=updated; trigger=b; reason=Add the untested nonlinear residual-profile posterior category while retaining the existing source-only acquisition and evidence restrictions.\n  - evidence: Historical cycle-2 MAE 0.0350330335336673 versus IRT 0.04121063683083198; no-calibration 0.03464729153264736 and no-diversity 0.05351526989144261. Acceptance was not established and its cause remains unknown. No new experiment. Considered repeated auditing, adaptive posterior acquisition, and calibration-only changes; selected a matched-prefix estimator intervention requiring no new observations. Hypothesis: group-balanced Rasch-shrunk source profiles and ability offsets can complement the linear predictor; model-based posterior spread is not target-calibrated uncertainty.\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- unknown_ts | step=unknown_step | scope=unknown_scope\n  - summary: (missing summary)\n  - evidence: (missing evidence)\n- 2026-11-13T17:51:56.142148+00:00 | step=evaluate | scope=attempt\n  - summary: harness evaluated program_1 exactly once\n  - evidence: combined_score=0.9684365684559878, correct=True; scientific acceptance passed; search metrics (data): {\"anchor_mae\": 0.24719956291422063, \"combined_score\": 0.9684365684559878, \"constant_mae\": 0.2040049293753487, \"control_failure_rate\": 0.0, \"copy_mae\": 0.19502341674926077, \"correct\": true, \"delta_anchor_ci_high\": 1.0, \"delta_anchor_ci_low\": -1.0, \"delta_anchor_mae\": -0.21563613137020848, \"irt_mae\": 0.04121063683083198, \"kendall_tau_b\": 0.75310530481357, \"mae\": 0.031563431544012165, \"missing_episode_rate\": 0.0, \"no_calibration_mae\": 0.12348718192012596, \"no_diversity_mae\": 0.05351873980080848, \"permuted_mae\": 0.12275843002570605, \"reset_mae\": 0.026756557227656522, \"reset_max_abs_error\": 0.0, \"rmse\": 0.041163281675283644, \"source_mean_mae\": 0.12786232844772225, \"spearman\": 0.8878296042522897, \"uniform_mae\": 0.09894661693226534}\n\n--- DRAFT TARGET LOCATIONS ---\n15:Predicting a language model's benchmark score from a few responses can reduce evaluation cost, but prediction accuracy and evaluation completeness are different requirements. We study a source-only estimator that selects items by their conditional covariance with the full score and combines ridge prediction with an optional Rasch-residual profile mixture. A frozen evaluation covers ten fixed benchmark cases, three grouped model splits, and budgets of 8, 16, and 32 items. On common available support, the estimator's mean absolute error decreases from 0.0439 to 0.0278 across these budgets; its Spearman correlation increases from 0.7787 to 0.8858. These are conditional descriptions, not qualified overall results. The evaluation completed but failed qualification: primary and reference predictions are missing for two Commonsense splits, and matched structural checks fail. The reported aggregate MAE of 0.0880 includes missing-output penalties. We separate measured prediction errors, scoring defaults, and unresolved diagnostics, establishing an evidence-bounded assessment rather than an overall selection-advantage claim.\n21:\\section{Introduction}\n26:We study this design together with a source-trained reconstruction family. A linear ridge predictor provides a simple fallback; a group-balanced mixture of Rasch-shrunk source profiles offers nonlinear response-pattern matching. Both use the same nested item prefixes, and their combination is selected using source-group holdouts. The scientific hypothesis is that source response structure can improve score reconstruction at a fixed query budget. The available evaluation does not isolate a benefit from the profile component, nor does it establish a generally advantageous selector.\n41:\\section{Related Work}\n46:Choosing observations for a scalar target relates to optimal allocation in regression \\citep{Elfving1952}, whereas information criteria for a whole parameter vector address a different objective \\citep{Kiefer1960}. Our empirical covariance rule is a regularized linear-prediction heuristic, not an optimal-design theorem for shifted binary responses. Ridge regression supplies a stabilized linear estimator \\citep{Hoerl1970}; standard statistical-learning and probabilistic-modeling texts provide broader background \\citep{Hastie2009,Bishop2006}. The profile model is a finite mixture, but it does not fit mixture weights by expectation maximization \\citep{Dempster1977}. Likewise, its fixed-ability difficulty fitting should not be confused with conditional maximum-likelihood estimation \\citep{Andersen1970}.\n49:Cross-validation distinguishes choosing a predictor from assessing it \\citep{Stone1974,Arlot2010}; evaluating a configuration on the same validation evidence used to tune it can be optimistic \\citep{Varma2006}. Grouped validation addresses dependence, but the blocking scheme determines which extrapolation question is tested \\citep{Roberts2017}. Domain-shift theory further motivates caution about transferring source accuracy to new response distributions \\citep{BenDavid2010}. Missing-data inference requires assumptions about the missingness process \\citep{Rubin1976,Little2019}; we make no such assumptions here. HELM motivates multi-metric evaluation \\citep{Liang2023}, and distinct benchmark constructions, such as MMLU-Pro, should not be conflated with the fixed MMLU case studied here \\citep{Wang2024}. These distinctions motivate reporting error, ranking, and evidence availability separately.\n51:\\section{Method}\n52:\\subsection{Problem Setup and Design Rationale}\n59:\\subsection{Score-Targeted Fixed Prefixes}\n76:\\subsection{Linear and Residual-Profile Reconstruction}\n86:The nonlinear branch retains source response profiles while smoothing them with a Rasch model. Source abilities are fixed at $\\theta_i=\\operatorname{logit}[(\\sum_jX_{ij}+0.5)/(N+1)]$. Item difficulties $d_j$ are fitted by group-weighted Bernoulli likelihood with a quadratic penalty. Write $r_{ij}=\\sigmoid(\\theta_i-d_j)$ and\n107:\\subsection{What a Fixed Prefix Can Identify}\n113:\\section{Evaluation Protocol and Evidence Availability}\n114:\\subsection{Fixed Benchmarks and Grouped Model Holdouts}\n115:The final assessment contains four Open LLM Leaderboard-derived cases (BBH, GPQA, MuSR, and OpenLLM Math) and six HELM-derived cases (Commonsense, GSM, LegalBench, MATH, MedQA, and MMLU). We retain these staged case names rather than asserting identity with every similarly named public benchmark. Each case uses a fixed binary item universe. The question is prediction for held-out models on that universe, not generalization to newly sampled questions or unseen benchmark distributions.\n124:\\subsection{Comparators and Control Semantics}\n130:The anchor reference clusters centered, normalized item response vectors and estimates scores from representatives weighted by assigned cluster sizes. The IRT reference fits a penalized two-parameter logistic response model, chooses items by fitted information near zero ability, and infers target ability from queried responses. These references use the same query budgets, but they are local comparators, not official reproductions of Anchor Points or tinyBenchmarks. A source-mean reference predicts the average source score without target responses. Extended fitting details are in the supplement.\n133:\\subsection{Three Distinct Reporting Objects}\n138:For conditional comparisons, all displayed methods must have predictions for a case--seed pair. We average budgets and targets within that pair and show its seed-level values. Pooled conditional summaries retain equal data-source and case weights, but normalize seed weights over available seeds \\emph{within each case}. The same availability intersection is used for error and ranking in the budget view. Commonsense therefore contributes only its available split, rather than being silently omitted or assigned a synthetic loss. This changes the estimand; it does not estimate missing performance. We show descriptive seed dispersion, not confidence bars. Spearman and Kendall correlations describe ordering \\citep{Spearman1904,Kendall1938}; neither establishes score calibration.\n141:\\section{Results}\n142:\\subsection{Completed Evaluation, Failed Qualification}\n191:\\subsection{Conditional Comparison Across Fixed Cases}\n205:\\subsection{Item Budget, Reconstruction, and Ranking}\n213:\\caption{Conditional error and ranking at each budget. Large dots use equal data-source and case weights, with available seeds normalized within each case. Small dots are descriptive seed summaries normalized over cases available for that seed; they are not independent replicates of the pooled estimator. Both panels and all methods use the same available case--seed intersection. No confidence interval or qualified overall comparison is implied.}\n221:\\section{Discussion and Limitations}\n226:The selected-item-mean condition supports a contrast between fitted reconstruction and no reconstruction on the primary prefixes. It does not isolate Rasch smoothing, residual profiles, group balancing, or their interaction. The fitted uniform control changes acquisition and allows downstream retuning, so it compares two configured procedures. Source-validation tuning establishes how settings are selected, not independent evidence that a component improves final performance. Sequentially developed configurations are likewise not controlled component interventions. Missing or unavailable ablations remain missing evidence.\n234:\\section{Conclusion}\n243:\\section*{LLM Usage}\n248:\\section{Supplementary Information}\n249:\\subsection{Inspectable Implementation and Reproducibility}\n280:\\subsection{Extended Estimation Details}\n281:Difficulty initialization uses the group-weighted mean ability minus the logit item mean. Item means are clipped to $[10^{-4},1-10^{-4}]$ for this initialization. Eight Newton updates use group-weighted Bernoulli residuals with difficulty penalty $0.01$ and clip each update to $[-2,2]$. Abilities remain fixed; this is not joint maximum-likelihood Rasch fitting. Profile probabilities are clipped with $\\epsilon=10^{-6}$ before applying offsets. Chunked particle summaries avoid retaining the full particle-by-item array during source tuning; a nonzero final blend stores the fitted particle probabilities. A zero blend bypasses that branch at prediction time.\n284:The source folds rebuild the selected order, Rasch probabilities, profiles, and priors on each fold's training groups. Linear configurations are chosen separately for each budget using equal-group squared error. The profile/blend grid uses MAE averaged over budgets, then rows within groups, then groups. It shares the validation folds with linear tuning, so this score is not an untouched outer-fold performance estimate. If only one source group is supplied, grouped tuning is unavailable and the code uses ridge strength one, shrinkage one, and a zero profile blend. This fallback is a code-defined behavior, not evidence that the final evaluator used a single-group fit.\n289:\\subsection{Local Reference Implementations}\n296:\\subsection{Available-Pair Numerical Results}\n353:\\subsection{Seed-Level Records and Exhaustive Numerical Ledger}\n413:\\subsection{Availability Masks and Statistical Interpretation}\n\n--- PROVENANCE SHAPE ---\n\"object\"\n[\n  \"count\",\n  \"generated_at\",\n  \"queries\",\n  \"references\",\n  \"retrieval_note\"\n]\n\n--- MEMORY LOG GUIDANCE ---\n\n**Update gate (the only valid triggers).**\n- (a) cycle **contradicts** an existing sentence → rewrite that sentence.\n- (b) cycle opens a **new category** not yet covered → add a sentence.\n- (c) cycle **flips a Do/Don't** recommendation → flip it.\n- (d) cycle **meaningfully refines** an existing sentence — narrows the conditions under which a rule holds, broadens its applicability to a config it wasn't known to apply to, sharpens a tentative claim into a confident one, or adds a qualifier the prior phrasing didn't cover → edit the sentence to incorporate the refinement. Simple re-confirmation in the same regime is **not** sufficient; you must identify the refinement dimension (narrow / broaden / sharpen / qualify) in `--gate-reason`.\n- otherwise → **keep**, do not invoke the helper.\n\n**Format constraints.** Single paragraph. ≤300 words. No blank lines (`\\n\\n`). Avoid detailed numerical figures — use qualitative thresholds (e.g. \"low LR\", \"small batch\") instead of precise floats like `LR=0.205`.\n\n**Update mechanism.** When execution is unavailable, apply the same validation rules\nand update the conclusions files directly with read/edit/write tools. When execution\nis available, use this helper invocation:\n```bash\npython \"${MEMORY_HELPER}\" --write-conclusions \\\n  --conclusions-md \"{{CONCLUSIONS_MD_FILE}}\" \\\n  --conclusions-history-jsonl \"{{CONCLUSIONS_HISTORY_FILE}}\" \\\n  --cycle-index {{CYCLE_INDEX}} \\\n  --worker-index {{WORKER_INDEX}} \\\n  --gate-trigger <a|b|c|d> \\\n  --gate-reason \"<one sentence; for (d) name the dimension>\" \\\n  --conclusions-text \"<the full new paragraph>\"\n```\n\n**Pre-flight self-check.** Before invoking the helper, count words (`len(paragraph.split())`) and confirm ≤300, and that the paragraph contains no blank line. Most validation rejections can be avoided here.\n\n**Retry budget — exactly 3 attempts per cycle.** On non-zero exit, read the stderr error, shorten the paragraph (drop the least-decisive sentence, merge two related sentences, or remove qualifiers), and retry. After **3 total attempts** with no success, the update is **discarded** for this cycle: do not retry further, do not write the rejected text anywhere, and append a single memory event with `step=\"conclusions_skip\"` whose `summary` names the last validation error. Underlying findings are not lost — they are already durable in `memory.md`.\n\n**Always log the gate decision.** Inside the regular memory append for the cycle, include `gate=<updated|kept|skipped>; trigger=<a|b|c|d|none>; reason=<one sentence>` in the entry's `summary` or `tags`. Use `skipped` only after the 3-attempt budget is exhausted.\n\n# Example evaluation entry\n```markdown\n### 2026-02-13T16:58:00Z | step=evaluate\n- program: program_3\n- combined_score: 2.54\n- correct: true\n- rubrics: uses_restarts=pass, constraint_optimization=pass, score_threshold=fail\n- evidence: late-stage overlap still visible in stdout trace\n- next_recommendation: raise late-stage overlap penalty and diversify restart seeds\n```\n\n--- WORKSPACE STATUS ---\nfatal: not a git repository (or any parent up to mount point /)\nStopping at filesystem boundary (GIT_DISCOVERY_ACROSS_FILESYSTEM not set).\n\n--- MEMORY FILES ---\nls: cannot access 'conclusions.md': No such file or directory\n-rwxr-xr-x 1 agent agent 14321 Nov 10 13:47 .codex/skills/memory-log/scripts/append_memory.py\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 27096 Nov 13 18:54 global_memory/memory.jsonl\n-rw------- 1 agent agent 25560 Nov 13 18:54 global_memory/memory.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent 12226 Nov 13 18:54 memory.md\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
